# Cray & Co., factors: up Chandler's Lane, lit, spotless, and minded by a clerk nobody sent home.
room counting_house "Cray & Co., Factors"
  bg bg_countinghouse_wide
  width 2560
  music music_office
  perspective horizon 300 ref 875 height 360
  walk (60,875) (110,752) (2450,752) (2520,875)
  entry 260,800

  # Atmosphere: Cray's lamps along the counting desks.
  footsteps wood
  light 415,490 radius 110 lamp
  light 663,490 radius 110 lamp
  light 1055,490 radius 110 lamp
  light 1328,490 radius 110 lamp
  light 1505,490 radius 110 lamp
  light 1858,490 radius 110 lamp
  light 2100,490 radius 110 lamp

  sprite npc_nib_body at 1130,770 size 0.95 idle speaker nib for nib grade "saturate(0.85) brightness(0.9)"

  hotspot desks "the counting desks"
    area 350,560 1550x180
    nowalk
    look "Five tall desks in a row, every pen lined up. Even the ink looks like it's been told to sit up straight."
    open "Locked, every drawer. The keys will be on a ring in Cray's pocket, alphabetised."

  hotspot pigeonholes "the pigeonholes"
    area 470,350 1230x205
    nowalk
    look "Hundreds of pigeonholes, numbered, each with a rolled paper. Bills of lading, salvage receipts, insurance. Other people's bad luck, filed."
    pickup "I reach for one, and Nib clears his throat without looking up. It's the most alarming noise I've heard all night."

  hotspot portrait "portrait of Silas Cray"
    area 1160,0 330x340
    nowalk
    look "Silas Cray, in oils, looking down at his own office. He looks as if he's already insured it against you."
    talk "I tell the portrait that it's going to have a very long morning. The portrait smirks. It was painted smirking."

  hotspot emblem "brass cloud"
    area 110,65 220x155
    nowalk
    look "The Cray & Co. cloud, in brass. The same cloud as on the kelp crates, and in wax on Rook's purse. A good mark for a man who sells fog."

  hotspot safe "the safe"
    area 2130,445 290x295
    stand 2080,800
    look "A black iron safe with a brass dial. What's inside is what Cray hid. What he thought harmless, he left on the shelves."
    open "I don't know the combination, and I'm not a clerk who guesses. The interesting books are in the pigeonholes, being boring."
    use "I don't know the combination, and I'm not the sort of clerk who guesses."

  hotspot tray "requisition tray"
    show if not has requisition and not has claims_book and not inquiry_done
    area 770,540 160x50
    stand 850,790
    item requisition
    look "An in-tray of blank requisitions on Nib's desk. CRAY & CO. REQUISITION: ITEM, QUANTITY, AUTHORITY. A little cloud at the top, smiling."
    pickup "I take a requisition and fill it in: one claims book, insurance, all of it. Authorised: Harbour of Port Vela. Nib doesn't look up."

  hotspot nib "Nib"
    area 1075,480 120x290
    stand 1330,800
    look "Cray's clerk: young, in an eyeshade, ink to the elbows. He's waiting for a clock to tell him he can stop. The clock hasn't."
    talk "He looks up from nothing in particular."
      talk nib
    give "“I can't take things. I can only take requisitions.”"
    state if has claims_book
      talk: talk nib at after

  hotspot door_out "door to the lane"
    area 95,330 210x415
    stand 240,800
    exit alley
    look "The door back out to Chandler's Lane. Polished on the inside too. Nobody polishes the inside of a door."

  use requisition on nib if req_stamped
    "I hand Nib the requisition."
    take requisition
    give claims_book
    sound chime
    talk nib at handed
  use requisition on nib
    "He turns it over, looking for something, and hands it back. “It isn't stamped. I can't not read it if it isn't stamped.”"
  use stamp on nib
    "He holds out the back of his hand, considers it, and withdraws it. “No. Then I'd be authorised. I don't know what I'd do.”"
  use compass on nib
    "“It's pointing at the wall.” It is. Past the wall is the reef. He doesn't ask."
  use ledger on nib
    "“That's the harbour's. We don't keep the harbour's. We just pay it.” He hears himself, and frowns, faintly."
  use crowbar on safe
    "I measure the crowbar against the safe. The safe wins on every measurement, including morally."
  use stamp on pigeonholes
    "Stamping Cray's own filing would be very satisfying and of no use whatsoever. I'll stamp something that counts."
